/// the processors `bar` and `baz`. Messages that do not fail for the processor `foo` will
/// skip these processors.
///
/// When messages leave the catch block their fail flags are cleared. This processor is
/// useful for when it's possible to recover failed messages, or when special actions
/// (such as logging/metrics) are required before dropping them.
///
/// > **Note:** When strict error handling (`error_handling.strict`) is enabled this
/// > processor does not recover anything, as a failed message short-circuits past it
/// > rather than reaching it. Use the
/// > [`try_catch`](https://docs.redpanda.com/redpanda-connect/components/processors/try_catch)
/// > processor instead, which contains both the fallible step and its recovery.
